# HyperFrames video projects: track the sources, ignore the output.
#
# Everything ignored here is regenerable from what IS tracked:
#   renders   -> `npm run render` in the project dir
#   snapshots -> `hyperframes snapshot`
#   captures  -> re-shot from the Storybook fixture stories
#
# The ignored files stay on disk. They are just not in git, because ~100 MB of
# mp4 that any clone can rebuild does not belong in the extension's history.
# Tracked instead: index.html compositions, hyperframes.json, package.json,
# meta.json, the sidebar build pipeline and its raw captures, fonts, icons.

# The repo root .gitignore excludes `coverage/` for test-coverage output, which
# would otherwise swallow the whole feature-clips/coverage/ composition.
# Re-include it here; the rules below still apply inside it.
!feature-clips/coverage/

# Rendered video, animation and audio output
**/renders/

# Frame grabs and contact sheets from `hyperframes snapshot`
**/snapshots/

# Screenshots captured off the running extension / Storybook stories
**/assets/captures/

# Intermediate fragments from assets/sidebar/build.cjs.
# The .raw.html inputs are tracked: those come from a hand-driven VS Code
# devtools session and no script in this repo can reproduce them.
**/assets/sidebar/*.frag.html
